---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="제주 월비 (WOLBI Jeju) — Word of Life Korea"
  description="제주 월비 — 대학 수준의 성경 교육과 제자훈련, 그리고 세계를 경험하는 11개월"
  activeNav="ministry"
>

<!-- WOLBI Jeju 본문 | 한/영 이중언어 (언어 표시/숨김은 global.css 가 맡는다) -->
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com">
<link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin>
<link href="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/pretendard@latest/dist/web/variable/pretendardvariable-dynamic-subset.css" rel="stylesheet">

<PageHero mark="WOLBI" image="/images/wolbi-jeju/hero-campus-spring-2026.jpeg" pos="50% 45%">
  <Fragment slot="eyebrow"><span class="wl-ko">제주 월비</span><span class="wl-en">WOLBI Jeju</span></Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="title">
    <span class="wl-ko">성경을 삶으로 <br class="ph-br">살아내는 1년</span>
    <span class="wl-en">One Year of Living the Word</span>
  </Fragment>
  <Fragment slot="bar">
    <p class="ph-sub">
      <span class="wl-ko">대학 수준의 성경 교육과 제자훈련, <br>그리고 세계를 경험하는 11개월.</span>
      <span class="wl-en">11 months of college-level Bible education, discipleship training, and global experience.</span>
    </p>
    <div class="ph-actions">
      <a href="https://www.wolbijeju.org/?lang=ko" class="ph-cta"><span class="wl-ko">더 알아보기</span><span class="wl-en">Learn More</span><svg aria-hidden="true" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none"><path d="M2 8h11M9 4l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="square"/></svg></a>
      <a href="/camp-register/" class="ph-cta ph-cta--ghost"><span class="wl-ko">캠프 참여하기</span><span class="wl-en">Join Camp</span></a>
    </div>
    <dl class="ph-stats ph-stats--text">
      <div class="ph-stat"><dt><span class="wl-ko">집중 성경 커리큘럼</span><span class="wl-en">Intensive Bible Curriculum</span></dt><dd><span class="wl-ko">11개월</span><span class="wl-en">11 Months</span></dd></div>
      <div class="ph-stat"><dt><span class="wl-ko">세계 10개 캠퍼스 네트워크</span><span class="wl-en">Global Network of 10 Campuses</span></dt><dd><span class="wl-ko">5개 대륙</span><span class="wl-en">5 Continents</span></dd></div>
      <div class="ph-stat"><dt><span class="wl-ko">미국 공인 기독교 대학 인증</span><span class="wl-en">U.S. Accredited Christian Institution</span></dt><dd>TRACS</dd></div>
      <div class="ph-stat"><dt><span class="wl-ko">선교 여행 (태국·베트남·이스라엘)</span><span class="wl-en">Mission Trips (Thailand · Vietnam · Israel)</span></dt><dd><span class="wl-ko">3개국</span><span class="wl-en">3 Countries</span></dd></div>
    </dl>
  </Fragment>
</PageHero>

<div class="wj-wrap" id="wl-root">

<!-- INTRO — 큰 사진 + 소개 글 -->
<section class="wj-sec wj-intro">
  <div class="wj-shell wj-split">
    <figure class="wj-split-media">
      <img src="https://wolko.synology.me/Jeju_WOLBI/Drone/campus2.jpg" alt="제주 월비 캠퍼스 전경" loading="lazy">
    </figure>
    <div class="wj-split-body">
      <p class="wj-eyebrow"><span class="wl-ko">WOLBI JEJU 소개</span><span class="wl-en">ABOUT WOLBI JEJU</span></p>
      <h2 class="wj-h2">
        <span class="wl-ko">아름다운 제주에서<br>성경의 깊이를 만나다</span>
        <span class="wl-en">Encounter the Depths<br>of Scripture on Jeju Island</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="wj-lead">
        <span class="wl-ko">제주 월비(WOLBI, Word of Life Bible Institute)는 대학교 과정에 준하는 체계적인 성경 교육과 제자훈련을 통해, 하나님의 말씀 위에 굳게 세워진 다음 세대를 준비시키는 사역입니다.</span>
        <span class="wl-en">WOLBI Jeju (Word of Life Bible Institute) is a ministry that prepares the next generation to stand firmly on God's Word, through systematic Bible education and discipleship training at the college level.</span>
      </p>
      <p class="wj-text">
        <span class="wl-ko">세계 5개 대륙 10개 캠퍼스 네트워크의 일부로서, 제주 캠퍼스는 한국·미국·캐나다·대만·일본 등 각국의 청년들이 11개월 동안 성경 66권과 조직신학 전 과정을 함께 배우고, 선교 여행과 사역 훈련을 통해 삶의 변화를 경험하는 곳입니다.</span>
        <span class="wl-en">As part of a global network spanning 10 campuses across 5 continents, the Jeju campus brings together young people from Korea, the United States, Canada, Taiwan, Japan, and beyond — studying all 66 books of the Bible and the full scope of systematic theology over 11 months, while experiencing life transformation through mission trips and ministry training.</span>
      </p>
      <blockquote class="wj-quote">
        <p class="wj-quote-text wl-ko">“월비에서 보낸 1년은 제 생애 최고의 해였습니다.”</p>
        <p class="wj-quote-text wl-en">“The year I spent at WOLBI was the best year of my life.”</p>
        <p class="wj-quote-source wl-ko">— 졸업생 간증</p>
        <p class="wj-quote-source wl-en">— WOLBI Graduate</p>
      </blockquote>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- HIGHLIGHTS — 네 가지 특징 -->
<section class="wj-sec wj-sec--soft wj-highlights">
  <div class="wj-shell">
    <div class="wj-head wj-head--split">
      <div>
        <p class="wj-eyebrow"><span class="wl-ko">제주 월비의 특징</span><span class="wl-en">Highlights</span></p>
        <h2 class="wj-h2">
          <span class="wl-ko">제주 월비만의<br>특별한 경험</span>
          <span class="wl-en">What Makes<br>WOLBI Jeju Unique</span>
        </h2>
      </div>
      <p class="wj-head-copy">
        <span class="wl-ko">1년간 말씀을 배우고, 사역 안에서 성장하고, 다양한 문화를 경험해 보세요.</span>
        <span class="wl-en">Study the Word, grow through ministry, and experience the world — all in one year.</span>
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="wj-hl-grid">
      <div class="wj-hl">
        <p class="wj-hl-num">66</p>
        <h3 class="wj-hl-label"><span class="wl-ko">성경 전권 학습</span><span class="wl-en">All 66 Books</span></h3>
        <p class="wj-hl-desc">
          <span class="wl-ko">구약·신약 전 66권을 세계적 성경 학자들에게 직접 배우며, 연간 성경을 3독에 가깝게 읽어냅니다.</span>
          <span class="wl-en">Study all 66 books of the Old and New Testaments under world-class Bible scholars, reading through nearly the entire Bible three times over the course of the year.</span>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="wj-hl">
        <p class="wj-hl-num">3</p>
        <h3 class="wj-hl-label"><span class="wl-ko">해외 선교 여행</span><span class="wl-en">Mission Trips</span></h3>
        <p class="wj-hl-desc">
          <span class="wl-ko">태국·베트남 선교 여행(12월), 이스라엘 성지 순례(3월)로 하나님의 말씀이 살아있는 현장을 직접 경험합니다.</span>
          <span class="wl-en">Mission trips to Thailand and Vietnam in December, and a Holy Land pilgrimage to Israel in March — experience the living Word in the places where it all happened.</span>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="wj-hl">
        <p class="wj-hl-num"><span class="wl-ko">다문화</span><span class="wl-en">Global</span></p>
        <h3 class="wj-hl-label"><span class="wl-ko">다국적 학생 공동체</span><span class="wl-en">Multicultural Community</span></h3>
        <p class="wj-hl-desc">
          <span class="wl-ko">북미 1/3, 한국 1/3, 아시아·기타 1/3로 구성된 다양한 문화권의 청년들이 함께 신앙 공동체를 이룹니다.</span>
          <span class="wl-en">Roughly one-third from North America, one-third from Korea, and one-third from Asia and beyond — a vibrant, faith-filled community from around the world.</span>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="wj-hl">
        <p class="wj-hl-num"><span class="wl-ko">대학</span><span class="wl-en">Credit</span></p>
        <h3 class="wj-hl-label"><span class="wl-ko">학점 인정 교육과정</span><span class="wl-en">College Credit Transfer</span></h3>
        <p class="wj-hl-desc">
          <span class="wl-ko">미국·캐나다 대부분의 기독교 대학에서 1년 학점으로 인정되며, 뉴욕 본교 2학년으로의 편입도 가능합니다.</span>
          <span class="wl-en">Credits are recognized at most Christian colleges in the U.S. and Canada, and transfer as a full first year. Students may also transfer directly into the second year at the New York home campus.</span>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ACADEMICS — 왼쪽 설명 + 입학 요건, 오른쪽 과목 목록 -->
<section class="wj-sec wj-academics">
  <div class="wj-shell wj-acad-layout">
    <div class="wj-acad-side">
      <p class="wj-eyebrow">ACADEMICS</p>
      <h2 class="wj-h2">
        <span class="wl-ko">깊이 있는<br>성경 커리큘럼</span>
        <span class="wl-en">In-Depth<br>Bible Curriculum</span>
      </h2>
      <p class="wj-text">
        <span class="wl-ko">2학기와 여름 사역 실습으로 구성된 집중 과정입니다. 구약·신약 전권, 조직신학 전 분야를 세계적 교수진과 함께 영어로 학습합니다.</span>
        <span class="wl-en">An intensive program structured around two semesters and a summer ministry practicum. All courses — covering the full Old and New Testaments and every area of systematic theology — are taught in English by world-class faculty.</span>
      </p>
      <div class="wj-facts">
        <p class="wj-facts-label"><span class="wl-ko">입학 요건</span><span class="wl-en">Admission Requirements</span></p>
        <ul class="wj-facts-list">
          <li><span class="wl-ko">고등학교 졸업자 이상 (3학년 졸업예정자 포함)</span><span class="wl-en">High school graduate or graduating senior</span></li>
          <li><span class="wl-ko">TOEFL 통과 또는 SYME 수료 후 MPT 통과</span><span class="wl-en">TOEFL score, or completion of SYME with MPT passage</span></li>
          <li><span class="wl-ko">Duolingo 90점 이상 (영어 비모국어 학생)</span><span class="wl-en">Duolingo score of 90 or higher (non-native English speakers)</span></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
    <ol class="wj-courses">
      <li class="wj-course">
        <span class="wj-course-num">01</span>
        <div class="wj-course-body">
          <p class="wj-course-tag"><span class="wl-ko">구약</span><span class="wl-en">Old Testament</span></p>
          <h3 class="wj-course-name"><span class="wl-ko">구약 개관 (Old Testament Survey)</span><span class="wl-en">Old Testament Survey</span></h3>
          <p class="wj-course-desc">
            <span class="wl-ko">창세기부터 말라기까지 전 39권의 배경, 주제, 핵심 교리를 개관합니다. 각 권의 정경적 기여와 주요 난해 구절을 포함합니다.</span>
            <span class="wl-en">A survey of all 39 books from Genesis to Malachi, covering their historical backgrounds, central themes, and key doctrines — including each book's canonical contribution and major interpretive challenges.</span>
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="wj-course">
        <span class="wj-course-num">02</span>
        <div class="wj-course-body">
          <p class="wj-course-tag"><span class="wl-ko">신약</span><span class="wl-en">New Testament</span></p>
          <h3 class="wj-course-name"><span class="wl-ko">신약 개관 (New Testament Survey)</span><span class="wl-en">New Testament Survey</span></h3>
          <p class="wj-course-desc">
            <span class="wl-ko">마태복음부터 요한계시록까지 전 27권을 다루며, 각 서신의 배경·신학·적용을 중심으로 학습합니다.</span>
            <span class="wl-en">A comprehensive study of all 27 books from Matthew to Revelation, with an emphasis on the background, theology, and practical application of each letter and narrative.</span>
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="wj-course">
        <span class="wj-course-num">03</span>
        <div class="wj-course-body">
          <p class="wj-course-tag"><span class="wl-ko">신학</span><span class="wl-en">Theology</span></p>
          <h3 class="wj-course-name"><span class="wl-ko">조직신학 1 — 신론·성경론·인간론·기독론·죄론</span><span class="wl-en">Systematic Theology 1 — Theology Proper, Bibliology, Anthropology, Christology, Hamartiology</span></h3>
          <p class="wj-course-desc">
            <span class="wl-ko">하나님의 본성, 성경의 권위와 무오성, 인간의 창조와 타락, 그리스도의 인격과 사역을 체계적으로 학습합니다.</span>
            <span class="wl-en">A systematic study of the nature of God, the authority and inerrancy of Scripture, the creation and fall of humanity, and the person and work of Jesus Christ.</span>
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="wj-course">
        <span class="wj-course-num">04</span>
        <div class="wj-course-body">
          <p class="wj-course-tag"><span class="wl-ko">신학</span><span class="wl-en">Theology</span></p>
          <h3 class="wj-course-name"><span class="wl-ko">조직신학 2 — 구원론·천사론·성령론·교회론·종말론</span><span class="wl-en">Systematic Theology 2 — Soteriology, Angelology, Pneumatology, Ecclesiology, Eschatology</span></h3>
          <p class="wj-course-desc">
            <span class="wl-ko">구원의 전 과정, 천사와 마귀, 성령의 사역, 교회의 설계, 말세 사건을 디스펜세이션 신학 관점으로 연구합니다.</span>
            <span class="wl-en">An exploration of the full arc of salvation, angels and demonic beings, the ministry of the Holy Spirit, the design of the church, and end-times events — studied from a dispensational theological framework.</span>
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="wj-course">
        <span class="wj-course-num">05</span>
        <div class="wj-course-body">
          <p class="wj-course-tag"><span class="wl-ko">서신서</span><span class="wl-en">Epistles</span></p>
          <h3 class="wj-course-name"><span class="wl-ko">로마서 · 갈라디아서 · 에베소서</span><span class="wl-en">Romans · Galatians · Ephesians</span></h3>
          <p class="wj-course-desc">
            <span class="wl-ko">복음의 논리와 신학적 적용(로마서), 믿음으로 말미암은 의(갈라디아서), 교회와 그리스도인의 삶(에베소서)을 심층 연구합니다.</span>
            <span class="wl-en">In-depth study of the logic and theological application of the Gospel (Romans), justification by faith alone (Galatians), and the church and the Christian life (Ephesians).</span>
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="wj-course">
        <span class="wj-course-num">06</span>
        <div class="wj-course-body">
          <p class="wj-course-tag"><span class="wl-ko">예언서</span><span class="wl-en">Prophecy</span></p>
          <h3 class="wj-course-name"><span class="wl-ko">예언서 — 다니엘 · 요한계시록</span><span class="wl-en">Prophetic Books — Daniel &amp; Revelation</span></h3>
          <p class="wj-course-desc">
            <span class="wl-ko">다니엘서를 통해 디스펜세이션 신학의 기초를 세우고, 계시록의 기호와 상징들을 예언적 틀 안에서 해석합니다.</span>
            <span class="wl-en">Building a dispensational theological foundation through Daniel, then interpreting the signs and symbols of Revelation within a coherent prophetic framework.</span>
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
      <li class="wj-course">
        <span class="wj-course-num">07</span>
        <div class="wj-course-body">
          <p class="wj-course-tag"><span class="wl-ko">실습</span><span class="wl-en">Practicum</span></p>
          <h3 class="wj-course-name"><span class="wl-ko">사역 실습 (Ministry Training)</span><span class="wl-en">Ministry Training Practicum</span></h3>
          <p class="wj-course-desc">
            <span class="wl-ko">캠프 사역, 교회 및 학교 방문, 전도, 지역사회 섬김 등 실제 사역 현장에서 말씀을 삶으로 적용하는 훈련을 받습니다.</span>
            <span class="wl-en">Hands-on training in real ministry contexts — including camp ministry, church and school outreach, evangelism, and community service — where students learn to apply the Word to everyday life.</span>
          </p>
        </div>
      </li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- TRIPS — 사진 세 장 -->
<section class="wj-sec wj-sec--soft wj-trips">
  <div class="wj-shell">
    <div class="wj-head">
      <p class="wj-eyebrow">STUDY TRIPS</p>
      <h2 class="wj-h2">
        <span class="wl-ko">세계로 나가는<br>성경의 현장</span>
        <span class="wl-en">Taking the Word<br>to the World</span>
      </h2>
    </div>
    <div class="wj-trips-grid">
      <article class="wj-trip">
        <div class="wj-trip-media">
          <img src="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Jerusalem%20Old%20City%20Western%20Wall%20%28Wailing%20Wall%2C%20Kotel%2C%20or%20Buraq%20Wall%29%20%2829305986108%29.jpg?width=1200" alt="이스라엘 예루살렘 서쪽 벽" loading="lazy">
        </div>
        <p class="wj-trip-when"><span class="wl-ko">매년 3월</span><span class="wl-en">Every March</span></p>
        <h3 class="wj-trip-title"><span class="wl-ko">이스라엘 성지 순례</span><span class="wl-en">Israel Holy Land Pilgrimage</span></h3>
        <p class="wj-trip-desc">
          <span class="wl-ko">10일간 전문 가이드와 함께 50여 곳의 성경 속 현장을 직접 방문합니다. 예루살렘, 갈릴리, 사해 등 성경 이야기의 배경이 살아 숨쉬는 땅을 걷습니다.</span>
          <span class="wl-en">Over 10 days, students visit more than 50 biblical sites with expert guides — walking through Jerusalem, Galilee, the Dead Sea, and the living landscapes that breathe life into the pages of Scripture.</span>
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="wj-trip">
        <div class="wj-trip-media">
          <img src="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Wat%20Phra%20That%20Doi%20Suthep%20%28I%29.jpg?width=1200" alt="태국 치앙마이 도이수텝 사원" loading="lazy">
        </div>
        <p class="wj-trip-when"><span class="wl-ko">매년 12월</span><span class="wl-en">Every December</span></p>
        <h3 class="wj-trip-title"><span class="wl-ko">태국 선교 여행</span><span class="wl-en">Thailand Mission Trip</span></h3>
        <p class="wj-trip-desc">
          <span class="wl-ko">태국의 다양한 선교 단체들을 방문하며 세계 선교의 현장을 경험합니다. 직접 사역에 참여하며 선교적 삶의 의미를 깨닫는 시간입니다.</span>
          <span class="wl-en">Students visit a range of mission organizations across Thailand, stepping into the front lines of global missions. Through hands-on involvement in ministry, they discover the meaning of a life devoted to the Gospel.</span>
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="wj-trip">
        <div class="wj-trip-media">
